# PATENT CLAIM LANGUAGE - SCANNING PROBE MICROSCOPE POSITIONING DEVICE

## Claim 1 (Independent Claim)

A positioning apparatus for a scanning probe microscope, comprising:

a base assembly configured to support a sample to be examined;

a bridge support structure extending upwardly from said base assembly, said bridge support having a first end and a second end, wherein said first end is fixedly mounted to said base assembly;

a scan head assembly configured to carry a probe tip for interaction with a sample surface, said scan head assembly comprising a housing containing piezoelectric scanning elements operatively coupled to said probe tip;

a parallel arm mechanism operatively interposed between said bridge support structure and said scan head assembly, said parallel arm mechanism comprising:

  a first arm member having a proximal end and a distal end;

  a second arm member having a proximal end and a distal end, said second arm member disposed in substantially parallel relation to said first arm member;

  a first hinge assembly rotatably coupling said proximal end of said first arm member to said bridge support structure at a first pivot axis;

  a second hinge assembly rotatably coupling said proximal end of said second arm member to said bridge support structure at a second pivot axis, said second pivot axis being substantially parallel to said first pivot axis and spaced apart therefrom by a predetermined distance;

  a third hinge assembly rotatably coupling said distal end of said first arm member to said scan head assembly at a third pivot axis;

  a fourth hinge assembly rotatably coupling said distal end of said second arm member to said scan head assembly at a fourth pivot axis, said fourth pivot axis being substantially parallel to said third pivot axis;

wherein said first, second, third, and fourth pivot axes are configured such that said first arm member and said second arm member, together with said bridge support structure and said scan head assembly, define a four-bar parallelogram linkage;

whereby actuation of said parallel arm mechanism causes said scan head assembly to translate along an arcuate path while maintaining a substantially constant angular orientation relative to said sample surface, thereby permitting coarse positioning of said probe tip relative to said sample without altering the tilt angle of said scan head assembly.

---

## Claim 2 (Dependent)

The apparatus of Claim 1, wherein each of said first, second, third, and fourth hinge assemblies comprises a flexure hinge formed from a monolithic reduced-thickness section of material, said flexure hinge providing rotational compliance about its respective pivot axis while substantially eliminating backlash and mechanical play.

## Claim 3 (Dependent)

The apparatus of Claim 2, wherein said flexure hinges are formed integrally with said first arm member and said second arm member from a unitary piece of metallic material selected from the group consisting of titanium, beryllium-copper alloy, and spring steel.

## Claim 4 (Dependent)

The apparatus of Claim 1, further comprising an actuator mechanism operatively coupled to said parallel arm mechanism, said actuator mechanism comprising a manually operable adjustment screw engaging at least one of said first arm member or said second arm member to effect controlled rotation about said first pivot axis or said second pivot axis, thereby producing translational displacement of said scan head assembly.

## Claim 5 (Dependent)

The apparatus of Claim 4, wherein said actuator mechanism further comprises a biasing spring disposed to maintain said parallel arm mechanism in engagement with said adjustment screw, said biasing spring urging said first arm member and said second arm member in a direction opposing an adjustment force applied by said adjustment screw.

## Claim 6 (Dependent)

The apparatus of Claim 1, wherein said bridge support structure comprises a substantially U-shaped or arch-shaped member defining an open region beneath said scan head assembly, said open region being dimensioned to accommodate said sample and permit optical viewing access to said probe tip and said sample surface.

## Claim 7 (Dependent)

The apparatus of Claim 1, wherein said predetermined distance separating said first pivot axis and said second pivot axis is substantially equal to a distance separating said third pivot axis and said fourth pivot axis, thereby ensuring said parallelogram linkage maintains true parallel motion of said scan head assembly throughout its range of travel.

## Claim 8 (Dependent)

The apparatus of Claim 1, wherein said arm members are configured with a length sufficient to produce an approximation to linear motion of said scan head assembly over a limited angular range of said parallel arm mechanism, said arcuate path exhibiting a vertical displacement component that is negligible relative to a horizontal displacement component over said limited angular range.

## Claim 9 (Dependent)

The apparatus of Claim 1, further comprising a locking mechanism configured to selectively immobilize said parallel arm mechanism at a desired position, said locking mechanism comprising a clamping element engageable with at least one of said first arm member or said second arm member to prevent further rotation about said respective pivot axis.

## Claim 10 (Dependent)

The apparatus of Claim 1, wherein said piezoelectric scanning elements comprise a piezoelectric tube scanner configured to effect fine positioning of said probe tip in at least one of an X-axis, a Y-axis, and a Z-axis relative to said sample surface, said fine positioning operating in conjunction with coarse positioning provided by said parallel arm mechanism.

## Claim 11 (Independent Claim - Method)

A method for positioning a scan head of a scanning probe microscope relative to a sample, comprising the steps of:

providing a bridge support structure fixedly mounted relative to a sample stage;

coupling a scan head assembly to said bridge support structure by way of a parallel arm mechanism comprising a pair of arm members each rotatably connected at opposing ends thereof via flexure hinge assemblies, said arm members and said flexure hinge assemblies forming a parallelogram linkage;

actuating said parallel arm mechanism to rotate said arm members about a first set of pivot axes proximate said bridge support structure;

translating said scan head assembly along an arcuate path in response to said actuating step, while maintaining said scan head assembly at a substantially constant angular orientation relative to said sample by virtue of said parallelogram linkage; and

positioning a probe tip carried by said scan head assembly into proximity with a surface of said sample for subsequent fine-scale scanning motion.

## Claim 12 (Dependent)

The method of Claim 11, further comprising the step of locking said parallel arm mechanism at a selected position by engaging a clamping element against at least one arm member of said parallel arm mechanism, thereby fixing said scan head assembly relative to said bridge support structure during a scanning operation.
